@title bit Generations - Orbital (Japan)
@file Bit Generations Orbital (J).gba
@game BVEJ
@chip SRAM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@save skip: nothing is written to SRAM through the menus and the first minute of stage 1 (the references leave blank 32 KB files, dingbat none); the first save needs a stage cleared, and steering the star into a captured orbit by A's gravity alone was not found by sight in the time given

# Health warning, A, the ORBITAL logo, START, "PRESS START", START, select
# galaxy 1, stage 1 (CLEAR TIME --:--), A: the stage. The star (the white
# dot the camera follows) drifts; A held for 120 frames pulls it onto the
# nearer red planet's orbit ring and it loses one of its five lives on the
# planet, then A for 30 more frames sends it drifting past a blue body.
# press_start: mgba a frame from dingbat and the second reference (IDENTICAL
# to each other) on the blinking "PRESS START": mgba alone.

[new]
wait 300
checkpoint warning window=30
press A
wait 300
wait 120
checkpoint logo window=30
press START
wait 120
checkpoint press_start window=30
press START
wait 120
checkpoint galaxy_select window=30
press A
wait 150
checkpoint stage_select window=30
press A
wait 200
wait 200
checkpoint stage1 window=30
wait 120
hold A
wait 60
wait 60
release
wait 60
wait 60
wait 120
hold A
wait 30
release
wait 30
wait 60
checkpoint drifting window=30
